 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to a quorum of the advisory\ncouncil on lead poisoning prevention",
    "basePrintNo": "S7150",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7150-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1370-b, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7150\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to a quorum of the\nadvisory council on lead poisoning prevention\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide that a majority of the appointed voting membership shall\nconstitute a quorum for the Advisory Council on Lead Poisoning\nPrevention.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 1370 of the public health law, by adding a\nnew paragraph 3 to provide that a majority of the Advisory Council on\nLead Poisoning Prevention's appointed voting membership shall constitute\na quorum.\n\nSection two provides an effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Advisory Council on Lead Poisoning Prevention has struggled to\nachieve a quorum due to a lack of appointees, which has obstructed the\nCouncil's ability to provide the guidance it was formed to produce.\nSimilar issues have arisen with other bodies and, as a result, amend-\nments to the functioning of the Transplant Council and the Early Inter-\nvention Coordinating Council were enacted in the last few years and have\nproven helpful. In 2019 the Governor signed legislation providing simi-\nlar relief to the State Camp Safety Advisory Council.\n\nThe General Construction Law Section 41 provides that, unless provided\notherwise, a government body's quorum shall be a majority of \"the total\nnumber which the...body...would have were there no vacancies and were\nnone of the persons or officers disqualified from acting.\"  Pursuant to\nGeneral Construction Law Section 110, this bill would exclude vacant\nseats and nonvoting members from the total number from which a majority\nis calculated.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nAn identical version of this bill was vetoed in 2019, however the very\nsame legislation provided for the State Camp Safety Advisory Council was\nsigned into law.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
